<title>GERMANY: German Hapag-Lloyd ups 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>German Hapag-Lloyd ups 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hamburg-based transport and travel company Hapag-Lloyd said on Friday it planned to increase its 1996 dividend to 18 marks per share from 16 marks the year before.</p>
<p>Hapag-Lloyd, which is quoted on the Hamburg stock exchange, said it was increasing its pay-out in line with business results and on the occasion of its 150th anniversary.</p>
<p>In November the group said it expected its 1996 operating profit to come in at 230-240 million marks compared to 265 million the year before. Full results are due in April.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
